The formation of a white precipitate upon mixing the sample with silver nitrate (\( \text{AgNO}_3 \)) suggests the presence of chloride (\( \text{Cl}^- \)) ions, as silver chloride (\( \text{AgCl} \)) is a common white precipitate.

Given the evidence from the flame test and the reaction with silver nitrate, the most likely identity of the unknown salt is sodium chloride (\( \text{NaCl} \)).

Final Answer: {"cation": "Na+", "anion": "Cl-"}
